## Securiti Background
Securiti was founded in 2019 by Rehan Jalil in San Jose, California. Its mission is to enable enterprises to responsibly harness the power of data and AI while maintaining trust, security, and regulatory compliance.

Securiti pioneered the category of Unified Data Controls with its flagship product Data Command Center, providing organizations with a single platform to discover data, classify it, protect it, and orchestrate compliance across multi-cloud, SaaS, on-prem, and AI environments.

The company had initially raised over $150M in funding from investors, including General Catalyst, Mayfield, and Wing Venture Capital, and has been recognized as a leader in data privacy and security automation.

##Veeam Acquisition and Strategic Integration
In late 2025, Veeam Software completed a definitive acquisition of Securiti AI for approximately $1.725 billion in cash and stock, a strategic move aimed at unifying data resilience, data security, privacy, governance, and AI trust capabilities into a single trusted data platform.
Under this acquisition:
- Rehan Jalil, Securiti founder & CEO, joined Veeam as President of Security and AI to lead the integration and expansion of combined security and AI offerings.
- The Securiti Data Command Center continues as a core part of the combined platform, giving customers unified visibility, security, governance, and recovery across production, backups, and AI pipelines at machine speed.
- The combined platform aims to accelerate safe AI adoption at enterprise scale by providing trusted, governed, and recoverable data, addressing a major cause of AI project failure.
- Veeam welcomed Securiti’s approximately 600 experts, expanding its capabilities in DSPM, privacy engineering, compliance automation, and AI trust.
This acquisition positions Securiti’s technology at the intersection of data protection (resilience) and security governance, enabling customers to secure, govern, and recover data seamlessly across environments, from structured applications to unstructured sources with AI-ready controls.


